# Praetor-managed artifacts whose bytes are pinned by .standards.lock digests or
# covered by an Ed25519 signature. Reformatting them breaks `praetorctl audit`
# with "lockfile digest does not match the archetype source".
#
# The list grew when switching prettier to tabs reformatted four of them at once
# and verify-all failed with "DevContainer out of sync with declared standards:
# recorded bootstrap configuration differs from declared profiles or contains
# unrecognized edits". The adopter's own formatter is enough to break the audit,
# and praetor does not declare these paths to it -- filed upstream.
.config/archetypes/
.standards.lock
.standards-receipt.json
.standards-baseline.json
.standards.yaml
standards.sublime-project
.devcontainer/
.github/rulesets/

# Generated lockfiles and build output
pnpm-lock.yaml
**/dist/
**/.svelte-kit/
**/storybook-static/
coverage/

# Vendor context projections generated by `praetorctl compile-context` from the
# canonical AGENTS.md. Formatting them here desyncs them from their source and
# fails the HISS-16 context-integrity gate on the next audit.
CLAUDE.md
.cursor/rules/
.github/copilot-instructions.md
.windsurfrules
.gemini/
.codex/
.claude/agents/
.github/agents/

# The HISS-20 fixture corpus is input to the rules, not source governed by them,
# which is why eslint.config.ts ignores it too. Its files are written to
# demonstrate a specific shape -- a function of a given length, an indentation
# the scanner measures -- so reformatting them would change the evidence the
# coverage catalog's claims are replayed against.
.config/hiss/testdata/
